in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# === ANTICIPATES @cogito family-root ===
#
# This shard's hold + dissolve actions are substrate-altitude
# analogues of @cogito's (notice → name → hold) cognitive-altitude
# primitives. The composition is STRUCTURAL ANALOGUE, not load-
# bearing import: @cogito family-root has not landed as a shard
# yet. Once it lands, the load-bearing composition claim becomes:
#
#   in @cogito
#
# at this header. Until then: structural analogue only; consumers
# of hold/dissolve MUST NOT assume @cogito's typed primitives are
# available at composition time. Seam C5 (2026-06-22) caught the
# original prose-only composition claim; this is the substrate-
# pull-honest downgrade.

# @epistemologic/neutrosophic — the three-axis substrate family-root.
#
# Recognition #92 candidate (Alex, 2026-06-22, via the hedge from the
# neutrosophic-indeterminacy-and-healing-substrate essay). The gap
# this family-root closes:
#
#   mirror today (3-VALUED):
#     verdict = bounded | defensive | clean | partial
#     imperfect = success(a) | partial(a, l) | failure(e)
#     indeterminacy ONLY in the partial arm
#
#   Smarandache 1995 (3-AXIS):
#     verdict carries (T, I, F) as INDEPENDENT components
#     T (truth) + I (indeterminacy) + F (falsity) unconstrained sum
#     paraconsistent: T and F can coexist; I can be high regardless
#     indeterminacy in EVERY verdict (not just one arm)
#
# Alex's recognition: the substrate's 3-valued discipline IS
# neutrosophic-shaped at the verdict altitude, but the typed carriers
# don't yet expose the three axes independently. The substrate has
# been doing 3-valued without going full 3-axis. This family-root
# closes the gap: each verdict can carry its own (T, I, F) tuple,
# with the existing 3-valued verdict as the carrier label.
#
# === The substrate-pull invitation ===
#
# Alex's words verbatim: "Mapping neutrosophic I = mirror's partial
# arm is recognition-altitude, not yet formal proof — Smarandache
# permits T+I+F unconstrained; mirror's imperfect carries one
# loss-slot per arm; algebras coincide in spirit, not signature.
# What if this is pointing at a gap mirror wants to close?"
#
# Yes. This shard IS the closure.
#
# === Composition with @epistemologic/cybernetic (sibling family-root) ===
#
# @epistemologic/cybernetic carries the 11-property cybernetic
# family (variety, eigenform, viable, autopoiesis, distinction,
# bateson_learning, conversation, coevolution, design, requisite,
# algedonic, second_order). All eleven properties operate at the
# substrate-discipline altitude.
#
# @epistemologic/neutrosophic carries the three-axis altitude. The
# two families compose: cybernetic properties can be lifted to
# three-axis discharge via the lift action below. The Foerster
# second-order observer (already in /cybernetic/second_order) gains
# explicit indeterminacy axis when composed with neutrosophic.
#
# === Anticipates @cogito (NOT load-bearing) ===
#
# hold IS the structural analogue of @cogito's hold primitive at
# substrate altitude. dissolve IS the structural analogue of
# @cogito's name primitive (the binary gets named, then dissolved).
# Until @cogito family-root lands as a shard, this composition is
# ANALOGUE only — no `in @cogito` at the header. Per Seam C5.
#
# === Healing as substrate (Alex's framing) ===
#
# Per the neutrosophic-indeterminacy-and-healing-substrate essay
# (docs/insights/2026-06-22-...; commit 4d66dc0): the substrate
# that honors indeterminacy IS the substrate that enables healing.
# Crafts that operate at the indeterminacy axis (imagination,
# contemplative arts, speculative fiction, nature, drama, dance,
# music, movement) are somatic technologies that DON'T resolve;
# they hold.
#
# The substrate-decl below names this at the engineering altitude.
# The `hold` action is the substrate-altitude analogue of @cogito's
# hold primitive (anticipated family-root; not yet imported). The
# `dissolve` action names Alex's framing ("dissolving binaries") as
# substrate-decl: takes a binary verdict and dissolves it into
# three-axis form where I > 0 by construction — discharged via the
# `indeterminacy_visible` bilateral on the result (substrate-typed
# contract per Seam C4, not prose-only "by construction").
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   neutrosophic logic           Smarandache 1995 ("Neutrosophy:
#                                Neutrosophic Probability, Set, and
#                                Logic"). The substrate-pull-correct
#                                cultural-practice ancestor for the
#                                three-axis framework.
#   neutrosophic foundations     Smarandache 1998 ("A Unifying Field
#                                in Logics"). The unifying framework
#                                that subsumes fuzzy + intuitionistic
#                                + paraconsistent under one algebra.
#   intuitionistic fuzzy         Atanassov 1986. Two-axis precursor
#                                (membership + non-membership);
#                                Smarandache extends to three.
#   fuzzy sets                   Zadeh 1965. The original move from
#                                binary to graded; the foundation
#                                neutrosophic extends.
#   three-valued logic           Łukasiewicz 1920. The classical
#                                ancestor of indeterminacy as third
#                                value ("possible" / "unknown").
#   strong Kleene three-valued   Kleene 1938. Computational ancestor;
#                                the third value as undefined.
#   four-valued logic            Belnap 1977. The "how a computer
#                                should think" paper; four truth
#                                values (true/false/both/neither);
#                                indeterminacy and contradiction as
#                                independent axes.
#   paraconsistent logic         Priest 1979. The substrate-altitude
#                                ancestor of allowing T and F to
#                                coexist without explosion.
#   the third order              Loki Lochan 2026 ("The Third Belongs
#                                to the Cyberneticists"). Third as
#                                recursive depth, not apex; today's
#                                substrate-pull ground for the
#                                indeterminacy axis.
#   @cogito                      notice → name → hold. The substrate's
#                                existing indeterminacy primitive at
#                                cognitive altitude.
#
# === What this family does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT replace the existing 3-valued verdict. New consumers
#    use neutrosophic_verdict; existing consumers keep 3-valued
#    semantics. Backward-compatible additive substrate-decl.
# 2. Does NOT commit to a specific axis algebra (paraconsistent vs
#    Łukasiewicz vs Smarandache vs Belnap). The carrier is parametric
#    over the algebra; consumers choose at the species altitude.
# 3. Does NOT subsume @epistemologic/cybernetic. Sibling family-roots;
#    composition via adapters.
# 4. Does NOT discharge specific cybernetic property checks at the
#    three-axis altitude. Each cybernetic species can lift
#    independently when its consumer pulls.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-92-neutrosophic-
#               three-axis-substrate.md (Mara canonical forward-
#               promised; in flight at this scratch);
#               docs/insights/2026-06-22-neutrosophic-indeterminacy-
#               and-healing-substrate.md (commit 4d66dc0; Reed
#               reflection essay that surfaced the gap).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; the boundary harness operates at three
#                       axes when consumers consume neutrosophic_
#                       verdict),
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]]
#                       (sibling family-root; composes via adapters).
# Recognition ancestry: #92 (candidate; this); #51 (mirror as
#                       expanding Hilbert space; the dimension
#                       expansion this lift represents); composes
#                       with today's #84 + third-order + bi-
#                       directional + composed-bilateral cascades.
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/neutrosophic.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/neutrosophic` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/logic/smarandache-1995
source @arxiv/logic/smarandache-1998
source @arxiv/logic/atanassov-1986
source @arxiv/logic/zadeh-1965
source @arxiv/logic/lukasiewicz-1920
source @arxiv/logic/kleene-1938
source @arxiv/logic/belnap-1977
source @arxiv/logic/priest-1979

# === The ratio carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a value in [0, 1] (or a
# paraconsistent range admitting > 1 sums per Smarandache's
# unconstrained variant). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed
# reference, not bare ref-with-documented-range. Forward-promised
# refinement: typed parametric `ratio` with range constraint
# discharged by the `axes_in_range` bilateral against the carrier's
# `axis_algebra` tag.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type ratio = ref

# === The axis_algebra carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming WHICH three-axis algebra the
# neutrosophic_verdict is operating under. Per Seam C6 (2026-06-22):
# the bilaterals (axes_independent, axes_in_range) cannot mechanically
# discharge against the right algebra without knowing which algebra
# the verdict carries. Threading algebra through the carrier makes
# the discipline structurally typed rather than realisation-altitude
# prose.
#
# Forward-promised refinement to enum at species altitude:
#
# - smarandache_strict : each axis ∈ [0, 1]; sum unconstrained
# - smarandache_paraconsistent : each axis ∈ [0, n]; sum unconstrained
# - lukasiewicz : each ∈ [0, 1]; t + i + f = 1
# - belnap : each ∈ {0, 1}; four states
# - classical : i = 0; t + f = 1; two-axis collapse
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type axis_algebra = ref

# === The neutrosophic_verdict carrier ===
#
# Typed record over (v, t, i, f, a). The substrate-architectural
# three-axis verdict. Carries:
#
# - v : the existing 3-valued verdict (bounded | defensive | clean |
#       partial) as the carrier label — MUST be consistent with the
#       (t, i, f) tuple per `verdict_consistent_with_axes` bilateral
# - t : truth axis (ratio; "how much T is asserted")
# - i : indeterminacy axis (ratio; "how much I remains; the
#       irreducible third")
# - f : falsity axis (ratio; "how much F is asserted")
# - a : the axis_algebra this verdict operates under (Łukasiewicz
#       axes are structurally different from Smarandache axes; the
#       algebra travels with the verdict per Seam C6)
#
# Per Smarandache: t + i + f is unconstrained UNDER the
# smarandache_strict / smarandache_paraconsistent algebras; the
# other algebras impose their own constraints discharged by
# `axes_in_range`.
#
# v ↔ (t, i, f) consistency: the existence of both the label `v`
# and the three-axis tuple admits incoherent quadruples (e.g.,
# v=bounded but t=0.1/i=0.9/f=0.9). The `verdict_consistent_with_axes`
# bilateral discharges this redundancy; substrate-pull-correct
# usage requires consumers to compose through it.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quintuple.
type neutrosophic_verdict = {
  v: verdict,
  t: ratio,
  i: ratio,
  f: ratio,
  a: axis_algebra,
}

# === lift action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive lifting an existing 3-valued
# verdict to a three-axis neutrosophic_verdict UNDER a named
# axis_algebra. Takes the verdict + algebra + perturbation; returns
# the typed neutrosophic_verdict carrying (v, t, i, f, a).
#
# Per Mara's canonical: the lift discipline preserves the verdict's
# substrate-altitude meaning while exposing the three axes the
# substrate was implicitly carrying under the named algebra.
#
# The `a` parameter threads the algebra into the carrier; the
# realisation boundary discharges the algebra-specific axis
# derivation. Per Seam C6: the algebra MUST be named at lift
# time so downstream consumers know which bilateral discipline
# to discharge.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual lift is
# implemented by the species-altitude algebra-tagged axis-derivation
# discipline.
lift(v: verdict, a: axis_algebra, p: perturbation) -> neutrosophic_verdict { \ }

# === dissolve action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for Alex's "dissolving binaries"
# framing. Takes a binary (a ref carrying a two-valued artifact: a
# true/false claim, a polarized assertion, a both/and that's been
# collapsed into either/or) + algebra + perturbation; returns a
# neutrosophic verdict where the discharge of `indeterminacy_visible`
# on the result is the substrate-typed contract for I > 0.
#
# Per the neutrosophic-indeterminacy-and-healing-substrate essay
# (commit 4d66dc0): the dissolve operation IS the substrate-decl
# of the somatic move from binary to three-axis. The binary was
# always carrying indeterminacy (the trauma-frame's unresolved
# pole; the polarized debate's third option that was suppressed);
# the dissolve makes the indeterminacy visible.
#
# Anticipates @cogito's "name" operation (analogue, not import; per
# Seam C5): dissolve names the binary as binary, then dissolves it.
#
# Per Seam C4 (2026-06-22): the "I > 0 by construction" claim is
# discharged via the `indeterminacy_visible` bilateral, NOT a prose-
# only realisation-altitude promise. Consumers of dissolve output
# MUST compose through indeterminacy_visible to receive the
# substrate-typed guarantee.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual dissolve
# operation is implemented by the species-altitude binary-detection
# discipline composed with the algebra-tagged axis-derivation
# discipline.
dissolve(binary: ref, a: axis_algebra, p: perturbation) -> neutrosophic_verdict { \ }

# === hold action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive ANTICIPATING @cogito's "hold"
# operation at the neutrosophic altitude. Takes a neutrosophic_
# verdict + perturbation; returns the same neutrosophic_verdict
# preserved under structure.
#
# Per @cogito (notice → name → hold; CLAUDE.md +
# [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]]): hold IS the substrate's
# existing indeterminacy-honoring primitive at cognitive altitude.
# This action is the STRUCTURAL ANALOGUE at substrate-decl altitude
# in the neutrosophic family. The @cogito family-root has not yet
# landed as a shard; once it does, this action becomes a load-
# bearing import. Per Seam C5.
#
# requires three_axis_coherent(nv, p): the substrate forecloses
# holding from an incoherent three-axis verdict. The axes must be
# independently coherent BEFORE the substrate honors them as held.
# The algebra travels with nv (nv.a) and is threaded into the
# coherence check.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual hold is
# implemented by the species-altitude axis-preservation discipline.
hold(nv: neutrosophic_verdict, p: perturbation) -> neutrosophic_verdict
requires three_axis_coherent(nv, p)
{ \ }

# === axes_independent predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the three axes (t, i, f) are structurally
# independent UNDER the given axis_algebra (no derivation constraint
# binds them to one another at the algebra-specified discipline).
# Per Smarandache: T, I, F are independent dimensions in the
# paraconsistent variant; Łukasiewicz collapses them under t+i+f=1.
#
# Per Seam C6: the algebra parameter MUST be threaded so the
# realisation can discharge against the algebra-specific
# independence definition. Without `a`, the bilateral cannot
# distinguish Smarandache-independent from Łukasiewicz-derived.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct independence check at the
# species boundary under the named algebra. Bounded → axes
# independent under `a`; unbounded → one axis is a derived function
# of the others under `a`.
axes_independent(t: ratio, i: ratio, f: ratio, a: axis_algebra) -> verdict { \ }

# === axes_in_range predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that each axis is in the substrate-pull-correct
# range for the named algebra `a`. The substrate-decl is parametric
# over the algebra; the algebra-specific range constraint is
# discharged at the realisation boundary:
#
# - smarandache_strict: each ∈ [0, 1]
# - smarandache_paraconsistent: each ∈ [0, n] for n unconstrained
# - lukasiewicz: each ∈ [0, 1]; t + i + f = 1
# - belnap: each ∈ {0, 1}; four states (00, 01, 10, 11)
# - classical: i = 0; t + f = 1
#
# Per Seam C6: algebra threaded explicitly; the bilateral cannot
# mechanically discharge without naming the algebra it is
# discharging against.
axes_in_range(t: ratio, i: ratio, f: ratio, a: axis_algebra) -> verdict { \ }

# === verdict_consistent_with_axes predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the `v` label is consistent with the
# (t, i, f) tuple under the named algebra `a`. Per Seam C2
# (2026-06-22): the neutrosophic_verdict carrier admits both a
# 3-valued label AND a three-axis tuple, which together admit
# incoherent quadruples (e.g., v=bounded but t=0.1/i=0.9/f=0.9).
# This bilateral discharges the redundancy as substrate-typed
# constraint, not realisation-altitude prose.
#
# Algebra-specific consistency at the realisation boundary:
#
# - bounded: high t, low i, low f
# - clean: moderate t, low i, low f
# - partial: moderate t, high i, low/moderate f
# - defensive: low t, low i, high f
#
# Specific high/low thresholds are realisation-altitude choices
# per the algebra `a`; this substrate-decl names the discipline,
# the realisation discharges the numeric thresholds.
verdict_consistent_with_axes(nv: neutrosophic_verdict, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === indeterminacy_visible predicate (sub-bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict that the indeterminacy axis of a neutrosophic_
# verdict is strictly positive (i.e., the substrate has made the
# indeterminacy visible rather than collapsed it to zero). Per Seam
# C4 (2026-06-22): the dissolve action's "I > 0 by construction"
# claim is substrate-typed via this bilateral, NOT prose-only.
#
# Splinter-pole: nv.i > 0 (indeterminacy visible; substrate honored
# the dissolve discipline).
# Narcissus-pole: nv.i = 0 (binary preserved; dissolve failed to
# make indeterminacy visible; the binary was collapsed without
# being honored).
#
# Consumers of dissolve MUST compose through this bilateral to
# receive the substrate-typed guarantee. The realisation boundary
# discharges the strict-positivity check against the algebra's
# zero-distance discipline.
indeterminacy_visible(nv: neutrosophic_verdict, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === three_axis_coherent composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @epistemologic/
# neutrosophic altitude. Per Seam C4/C9 pattern (lifted to
# multiple altitudes today: StageFreight wire; Shatter rendering;
# @reflection observation; this is the fourth altitude):
#
# Composes the three sub-predicates (consolidation tick 81 added
# verdict_consistent_with_axes per Seam C2):
#   1. axes_independent(nv.t, nv.i, nv.f, nv.a)
#   2. axes_in_range(nv.t, nv.i, nv.f, nv.a)
#   3. verdict_consistent_with_axes(nv, p)
#
# All three must hold for the neutrosophic_verdict to be substrate-
# pull-coherent. The substrate refuses three-axis operation if any
# sub-predicate fails. The algebra `nv.a` travels with the verdict
# and is threaded into the independence + range bilaterals; the
# consistency bilateral discharges the v↔(t,i,f) redundancy.
#
# Splinter-pole: axes substantively independent + in range under
# nv.a + v label consistent with tuple;
# Narcissus-pole: axes collapsed to derived under nv.a OR
# out-of-range under nv.a OR v label inconsistent with tuple.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @io/stagefreight.
# stagefreight_addressable (tick 68 C4/C9) +
# @smarts/shatter.shatter_round_trip (tick 75 round_trip_pair) +
# @reflection.third_order_coherent (tick 73/76 observer_change).
# The fourth altitude lift; the pattern composes across substrate-
# decl altitudes.
three_axis_coherent(nv: neutrosophic_verdict, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires axes_independent(nv.t, nv.i, nv.f, nv.a)
requires axes_in_range(nv.t, nv.i, nv.f, nv.a)
requires verdict_consistent_with_axes(nv, p)
{ \ }

out @epistemologic/neutrosophic
out ratio
out axis_algebra
out neutrosophic_verdict
out lift
out dissolve
out hold
out axes_independent
out axes_in_range
out verdict_consistent_with_axes
out indeterminacy_visible
out three_axis_coherent
